{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1773875449,"nonce":"YHdNLNmT98Evu6UlMRrMC8GV1Q0=","message":"Regression discovered 2026-03-18: auto-build skipped when feature branch contains a dist-restore commit.\n\nThe auto-build logic skips rebuild if `git diff --name-only \u003cpre-merge-head\u003e HEAD -- dist/ ui/dist/` is non-empty, assuming dist was already built. But this fires a false positive when an agent strips dist/ from a feature branch by doing `git checkout origin/main -- dist/ ui/dist/ \u0026\u0026 git commit` — that restore commit counts as a dist change, so auth-merge skips the rebuild even though dist is stale relative to the new src/ changes.\n\nTriggered by: feature/sdk-backend merge. Codex committed dist/ in the feature branch; Opus cleanup restored dist/ to main state as a commit; auth-merge saw the restore as a dist commit and skipped the rebuild. Result: daemon running old dist with none of the SDK backend changes.\n\nRoot cause: the skip condition conflates \"dist was changed\" with \"dist was built from current src\". A restore-to-main-state commit satisfies the former but not the latter.\n\nFix options:\n1. Change the skip heuristic: instead of checking whether dist/ changed at all, check whether dist/ changed AND the change is newer than the src/ change (e.g. check commit ordering, or compare content hash of dist against a fresh build).\n2. Simpler: require agents to never commit dist/ restorations — instead leave dist/ as unstaged/untracked on the feature branch so the auto-build correctly detects \"no dist commit\". Document this in CLAUDE.md: when stripping dist/ from a feature branch, do `git rm --cached -r dist/ ui/dist/` rather than restoring and committing.\n3. Even simpler: always rebuild if src/ changed, regardless of dist/ state. The extra build cost is minor.","files":null}]}